A||||1||SCCA FIERO||F.Y.I. extended life anti-freeze
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||06-17-99||09:53 PM||||I put extended life anti freeze in my 94 S-10 ZR2 with the enhanced 4.3. It destroyed my head gaskets and caused my heater core to leak(changing that thing SUCKED!!!) I was not aware of this and my father-in-law,a GM mechanic for 20+ years,informed me that extended life only belongs in cars that came with it(starting in 96 I think) or this will happen.
Z||000001||theogre||06-18-99||01:07 PM||||The primary component of antifreeze, ethelene glycol, does not break down. It will protect the system fromt freezing forever as long as it's in there in the right amount.The additive package that prevents corosion and oils the water pump is what gets stale. <p>As long as the system hasn't gotten full of crap, you can simply replace the additive pakage. Prestone and others have the products to do that.<p>This is alot of the reason you can recycle antifreeze. The machine that does it is basically a centrifigal seperator, and a filter. It simply seperates the glycol from the water, and filters out the particle matter. After treatment you just put in a new additive package and that's it.
